ow-to-mid 40s", "Turek's outside spending advantage offsets Hinson's cash-on-hand edge"], "rationale": "The polling average shows a narrow Democratic edge, but the freshest surveys from Emerson and SSRS put Hinson up two, and all three prediction markets lean Republican. With expert ratings overwhelmingly calling this a Tossup and the state's six-point Republican lean, the race sits at dead even.", "watch": "A second debate or late outside-spending surge could break the tie in either direction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Joni Ernst (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's open Senate seat is one of the closest races of 2026. Joni Ernst's retirement leaves a Republican-leaning state without an incumbent, and Democrat Josh Turek has kept pace with Ashley Hinson in fundraising while benefiting from heavy outside support. Recent polls are split: some show Turek narrowly ahead, but the two latest surveys put Hinson up two points.\n\nExpert raters call the race a Tossup almost unanimously, and prediction markets give Turek roughly a 43 to 47 percent chance. With the environment favorable to Democrats but the state tilted Republican, the race is genuinely even heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6012, "margin": 1.25}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5782, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5857, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5846, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.503, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.579, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5896, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5557, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.499, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5985, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.607, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6056, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_de